{
  "title": "Osteoporotic Vertebral Compression Fracture",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/spine/2021/osteoporotic-vertebral-compression-fracture",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jul 12 2026",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Osteoporotic vertebral compression fractures are very common fragility fractures of the spine that affect up to 50% of people >80 y/o",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis can be made with lateral radiographs. MRI or bone scan can help determine the acuity of a fracture",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is usually observation and pain management. Kyphoplasty is reserved for patients with recalcitrant symptoms after failure of nonoperative treatment for 4-6 weeks. Assessment and management of osteoporosis are indicated in the presence of these injuries",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "vertebral compression fracture (VCF) is the **most common fragility fracture**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "700,000 VCFs per year in the U.S.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "70,000 hospitalizations annually",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "$15 billion in annual costs",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "affects up to",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "25% people >70 y/o",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "50% people >80 y/o",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Risk factors",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**history of 2 VCFs**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "strongest predictor of future vertebral fractures in postmenopausal women",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathoanatomy",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "osteoporosis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "characteristics",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "bone quality is normal, but quantity is decreased",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "cortices are thinned",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "cancellous bone has decreased trabecular continuity",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "bone mineral density (BMD) in the lumbar spine",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "peaks at",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "text": "**females: 33-40 y/o**",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "4",
                              "children": []
                            },
                            {
                              "text": "**males: 19-33 y/o**",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "4",
                              "children": []
                            },
                            {
                              "text": "**peak BMD is widely variable based on demographic factors and location in the body**",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "5",
                              "children": []
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "decreases with age following peak mass",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "correlates well with bone strength and is a good predictor of fragility fracture",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "WHO defines osteoporosis as a **T score below -2.5**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**compromised pulmonary function**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "increased kyphosis can affect pulmonary function",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "each VCF can result in up to 9% reduction in FVC",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**increased risk of mortality from pulmonary dysfunction**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pain",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "25% of VCFs are painful enough that patients seek medical attention",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "pain is usually localized to the area of the fracture",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "may wrap around rib cage in a dermatomal distribution",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "focal tenderness",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "pain with deep palpation of spinous process",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "multiple compression fractures can lead to local kyphosis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "spinal cord injury (very rare)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "may see nerve root deficits with compression fractures of lumbar spine that lead to severe foraminal stenosis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "entire spine (concomitant spine fractures in 20%)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "will see loss of anterior, middle, or posterior vertebral height by 20% or at least 4 mm",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/2021/images/450px-l4_compressionfracture2008.jpg",
                  "caption": "Shows compression fracture"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "CT scan",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "usually not necessary for diagnosis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "fracture on plain films",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "neurologic deficit in the lower extremity",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "inadequate plain films",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "usually not necessary for diagnosis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "useful to evaluate for:",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "acute vs. chronic nature of the compression fracture",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "injury to anterior and/or posterior ligamentous complex",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "spinal cord compression by disc or osseous material",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "cord edema or hemorrhage",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "osteoporotic vs. metastatic etiology",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Studies",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Laboratory",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "a full medical workup (including CBC and BMP) should be performed",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "ESR may help to rule out infection",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "urine and serum protein electrophoresis may help rule out multiple myeloma",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Differential",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Metastatic cancer to the spine**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "must be considered and ruled out",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "the following variables should raise suspicion:",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "fractures above T5",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "atypical radiographic findings",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "failure to thrive and constitutional symptoms",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "younger patient with no history of a fall",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "observation, bracing, and medical management",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "majority of patients can be treated with observation and a gradual return to activity",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "PLL is intact (even if >30° kyphosis or > 50% loss of vertebral body height)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "if the fracture is <5 days old",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "calcitonin can be used for 4 weeks to decrease pain",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "medical management can include bisphosphonates to prevent future risk of fragility fractures",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "some patients may benefit from an extension orthosis (compliance can be an issue)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "however, several RCTs have shown similar pain, disability, and radiographic outcomes with or without a brace",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "-1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**vertebroplasty**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**indications**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "controversial",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "AAOS strongly recommended against the use of vertebroplasty in 2011, but then changed their stance in 2014 based on newer studies",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trials have shown no beneficial effect of vertebroplasty",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "vertebroplasty has higher rates of cement extravasation and associated complications than kyphoplasty",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "kyphoplasty",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "patient continues to have **severe pain symptoms after 6 weeks** of nonoperative treatment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "AAOS recommended that kyphoplasty may be used, but recommendation strength is limited",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "kyphoplasty is different from vertebroplasty in that a cavity is created by balloon expansion. Cement can be injected with less pressure into the cavity created by the balloon",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "pain relief is thought to be from elimination of micromotion",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "surgical decompression and stabilization",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "very rare in standard VCF",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "progressive neurologic deficit",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "PLL injury and unstable spines",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "to prevent possible failure due to osteoporotic bone",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "long constructs with multiple fixation points should be considered",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "consider combined anterior fixation",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Techniques",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Kyphoplasty vs. vertebroplasty**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "performed under fluoroscopic guidance",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "percutaneous transpedicular approach used for cannula",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "vertebroplasty",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "PMMA injected directly into cancellous bone without cavity creation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "performed when cement is less viscous",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "requires greater pressure because no cavity is created",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "increased risk of extravasation into spinal canal",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "kyphoplasty",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "cavity created with expansion device (e.g. balloon) prior to PMMA injection",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "performed when cement is more viscous",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "may be possible to obtain partial reduction of fracture with balloon expansion",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/2021/images/kyphoplasty.jpg",
                      "caption": "kyphoplasty"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Neurologic injury**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "can be caused by extravasation of PMMA into spinal canal",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "higher risk with vertebroplasty than kyphoplasty",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "important to consider defects in the posterior cortex of the vertebral body",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Vertebral body osteonecrosis (Kümmell's disease)**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "delayed post-traumatic osteonecrosis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
